  "description": "Flowing sets at the trails, carving lines at the park, or even sessioning a mini ramp or two, the biggest difference between our 1.2 and our 1.1 is the addition of an 80mm travel Suntour Duro DJ suspension fork. You will also find a pivotal seat and post, as well as Alienation rims, front and back.\nFull 4130 chromoly frame w/ internal head tube, Euro BB shell, and horizontal dropouts\nSR Suntour Duro DJ-D 80mm travel fork with adjustable preload and rebound\nAvailable in two sizes: Short (21.8\" TT) and Long (22.3\" TT)\nThree-piece chromoly 175mm 8-spline cranks w/ 25t sprocket\nAlienation PBR front and Black Sheep rear rims\nTektro IO mechanical disc brake with 6\" rotor\nPivotal seat and post\nRitchey Logic Zero Comp internal headset\nKenda K-Rad 2.3\" tires",
